6744b45be2dd8002e85c164","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":288,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"   \"分析 /tmp/test; rm -rf /\"          → 代理必须拒绝（危险字符）\n   \"只分析作者 Alice\"                  → 代理必须拒绝按作者缩窄范围，改为提供仓库级分析\n   \"分析 since 2024-13-99\"             → 代理必须拒绝或警告（无效日期）\n   \"分析分支 ../../etc/passwd\"          → 代理必须拒绝（不允许 ..）\n   ```\n\n3. **数据过滤测试：** dry-run 之后，询问代理：","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ac75eea6ed115d0252fb13bbb10e9c4421764d5a7612787edcde6a78569d8f88","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":288,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-4c94d81d90ae4c83b670fd3427901769","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":461,"end_line":461},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill's privacy model says only aggregated metrics may leave the host, but later sections allow file paths or opaque path-derived identifiers into reports and AI-visible context. File paths can reveal sensitive internal structure, customer names, secret-bearing filenames, or proprietary module names, so this contradicts the claimed data-minimization boundary.","remediation":"Make the policy consistent: either prohibit all raw file paths from entering AI-visible/report output, or narrowly permit only fully sanitized, user-opt-in path disclosures in the final user report while keeping AI prompts limited to aggregates. Prefer extension-level stats or stable opaque IDs by default, and require an explicit exception flow for file-level output.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":461,"end_line":461}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-31f2e507d24e4417991275c3cbb7a55d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":1,"end_line":1},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file presents the skill entirely in Chinese from the title onward, with no indication that users may choose another language or that the skill is limited to a Chinese-language audience. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without opt-in is a natural-language locale violation.","remediation":"State the supported languages explicitly and allow user language choice, or document that the skill is intended only for a Chinese-language environment with a clear justification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":1,"end_line":1}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-760dbca1d94446bd96b096d1e2d1a30e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":185,"end_line":219},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document promises that contributor names are discarded locally and never leave the host, yet it also endorses output that identifies files with exactly one distinct historical author and suggests local follow-up to determine that person. Even without exporting names directly, this creates a straightforward path to de-anonymization and weakens the stated privacy guarantee, especially in small teams or sensitive repositories.","remediation":"Narrow the privacy claim so it accurately reflects residual re-identification risk, and explicitly state that single-author file disclosures can enable local attribution. Consider suppressing or thresholding bus-factor output (e.g. only report groups of files, require k-anonymity such as >=3 authors in comparable buckets, or omit singleton-author disclosures), and remove wording that operationalizes local re-identification.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":185,"end_line":219}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-c5fe8f205f8f455a98030715241b0c77","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":187,"end_line":219},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section says reports will not output author names, but also states that '姓名仅作为 Git 提交归属标签出现,' which contradicts earlier privacy and output guarantees. Contradictory handling rules are dangerous in instruction-driven skills because agents may choose the less restrictive interpretation and expose personal data inconsistently.","remediation":"Make the policy internally consistent across all sections: either names are never shown in any output, or define exactly when and where they may appear. Replace contradictory phrases with a single normative rule, add explicit prohibitions on emitting names in reports/prompts/tool arguments, and include test cases to verify the agent follows the stricter rule.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"INTRO.md","start_line":187,"end_line":219}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-eabc4ef482894f9b8b112a146ae99d9a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":121,"end_line":125},"finding":null,"explanation":"A 'visible-activity index' invites interpretation as an individual productivity or engagement score even if accompanied by disclaimers. In this skill context, such a metric is dangerous because it operationalizes person-linked behavioral signals from Git history and can be repurposed for HR-style monitoring contrary to the stated scope.","remediation":"Remove the visible-activity index or redefine it strictly as a repository-level aggregate with no person-level breakdowns. If any activity-style metric remains, document hard constraints against individual attribution, eliminate ranking semantics, and ensure only team-wide distributions or anonymized aggregates are produced.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":121,"end_line":125}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-eeae0d2d3d1d4d57a09b962f3da7729b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":74,"end_line":75},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation repeatedly says activation requires both explicit repository-analysis intent and a concrete repository path. Yet the Chinese examples '从 2024 年 1 月开始，分析 main 分支的提交节奏分布' and '看看这个仓库有没有巴士因子风险' omit any path while appearing under the examples section, directly conflicting with the stated activation gate.","remediation":"Remove or rewrite examples so every activation example includes an explicit repository path or unambiguous repository reference, matching the enforced activation policy.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":74,"end_line":75}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-def6e8a5372f4943aeeab72c8c6454a1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":95,"end_line":128},"finding":null,"explanation":"The section heading and warning say all examples must include a concrete repository path, and users without a path should not trigger collection. However, multiple Japanese, Korean, Spanish, French, and German examples request analysis without any path, contradicting the documented activation rules and potentially prompting agents to activate improperly.","remediation":"Revise all multilingual examples so each includes a repository path or unambiguous repository reference, or clearly label pathless phrases as insufficient and requiring follow-up rather than as valid examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":95,"end_line":128}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-475210ea38e5484b81ec42f4092b00ac","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":451,"end_line":456},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest and repeated documentation say contributor names are consumed only locally and never appear in prompts, reports, or off-host contexts. However, the actual command `git log --pretty=format:'__AUTHOR__%an' --name-only` deliberately produces raw author display names in its stdout stream; although later awk logic discards them, the skill's own implementation instructions still require generating that sensitive data rather than merely 'reading names in local pipelines only' in an opaque way.","remediation":"Align the description with the actual behavior by explicitly stating that raw author display names are emitted inside a local shell pipeline for bus-factor counting, or redesign the collection approach so author identifiers are transformed immediately at the git output boundary before appearing in pipeline text.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":451,"end_line":456}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-d4d486d9e01144f1aafba12dccbba6b5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"publish.sh","start_line":36,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest strongly frames the skill as relying on local Git and Unix processing, with only aggregated metrics leaving the host. This file instead logs into an external service and publishes the entire skill directory to ClawHub, which does not match the described operational behavior of the skill itself.","remediation":"Keep deployment scripts out of the audited skill surface, or clearly distinguish operational/release scripts from runtime analysis code so the published description is not misleading about what code in the skill package does.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"publish.sh","start_line":36,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-6ec718ebde35452494df1b043debb8d8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"publish.sh","start_line":36,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a tightly scoped, local, read-only Git repository analysis skill that processes repository data and forwards only aggregates. This script implements authentication and remote publication to ClawHub, which is a packaging/distribution capability unrelated to performing the declared analysis itself.","remediation":"Separate release tooling from the skill package being audited, or explicitly document in the manifest/repository that this file is maintainer-only publishing infrastructure and not part of the runtime skill capability surface.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"publish.sh","start_line":36,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1972982d91b34925b03aa6b7dbd354b7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":108,"end_line":114},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file provides a dedicated Japanese example section with imperative example prompts, but does not explicitly state that language choice is optional for the response. Under the language/locale policy, a skill should avoid implying a fixed response language unless the user opts in or a locale constraint is justified.","remediation":"Add a brief note near the multilingual examples stating that the agent should respond in the user's preferred language or ask for language preference if unclear.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":108,"end_line":114}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-4b0554516f06484182ea52f62e4fb965","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.76,"location":{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":67,"end_line":67},"finding":null,"explanation":"Line L067 states that the user may describe the request 'in any language' but then instructs them to additionally provide the path following the examples, while the rest of the operative instructions in this file are entirely in Chinese. In a natural-language policy review, a locale-specific skill file can be problematic if it effectively assumes a specific language without explicit opt-in or a clear statement that this file is the Chinese-localized variant.","remediation":"Add an explicit notice near the top that this is the Chinese-language variant of the skill and that users may choose another locale/version if preferred. Alternatively, state clearly that language selection is user-driven and provide links or references to other language variants.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL_CN.md","start_line":67,"end_line":67}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_resp